MDRG METHOD: Lua Error-Driven Memory Scanning (Runtime Diagnostics via Forced Validation).
This method utilizes the game's embedded MoonSharp API and debugging system to reverse-engineer scene nodes.
The Lua script intentionally feeds an invalid or cross-scene path node to the texture manager.
During runtime validation, the embedded MoonSharp API rejects the false request and generates an error.
While handling the error, the manager dumps all legitimate target addresses into the text log.
These valid handles are exposed inside the "Potential matches" field within the txt log file.
This approach allows instant mapping of the RAM layout without relying on heavy external debuggers.
